R-FE4 R-SO6 R-SO19 R-FE2 R-FE3 R-LD4 R-CM3 R-RV1 (slice 064, `tln remove`): the compiler of `roc unbundle` in the ladder of `remove` is the compiler that the run holds, not the newest installed one (the follow-up of slice 060, G4).
One home with 3 compilers installed: `nightly-2026-10-14-38a3029` (the `roc:` pin of the header), `nightly-2026-10-12-2664a27` (the `default-roc` of `config.toml`) and `nightly-2026-10-16-9e9e9e9` (the newest). The project `r2` is the project `r2` of `remove/rm1-flow`: a platform, `json` 2.1.0 and `parser`, and a `roc:` pin. The package of `json` is NOT in the cache (the fake download and the fake `roc unbundle` make it, `fx/pkgs`).
Run 1 (`remove parser --file r2/main.roc`): the closure of the header after the removal needs `json`: one fetch (the download, then `roc unbundle`). The header has a pin, so the held compiler is the pin: `Fetch.selected({ held: <the pin>, default: <default-roc> })` is the pin. The `roc unbundle` job shows `toolchains/nightly-2026-10-14-38a3029/roc`: not the default (`2664a27`) and not the newest (`9e9e9e9`). The ladder then finds the new error of `json` (the probes of `fx/probes`): exit 10 (R-RV1), nothing is written.
